{
  "$description": "Palette catalogue \u2014 the named personalities a household app may adopt. Absorbed from the master project's standalone shadcn showcase (design-system#25), which had carried them since 2026-03-11 in the pre---ds-* namespace with every semantic surface declared outright.\n\nA palette is exactly TWO knobs, and cannot express a third:\n  accent  the primary action colour per mode, and ONLY that. Its -foreground pair is derived by the build (sd.config.js accentForeground: near-ink or near-white at the accent hue, whichever measures better against it), so there is no field an illegible pair could be written into.\n  tone    a hue plus a per-mode chroma SCALE, applied to the neutral ladder in tokens.tokens.json. The ladder's LIGHTNESS steps are package-owned and unreachable from here \u2014 they carry every contrast guarantee this package makes.\n\nThere is deliberately no field for a lightness, and none for a status colour: the status vocabulary (success/warning/error/info/neutral) is invariant across palettes, because a warning must read as a warning in every app.\n\nSee docs/development/decision-palette-catalogue-and-the-tone-axis.md for why this is two knobs rather than the showcase's full semantic override.",
